1
00:00:04,070 --> 00:00:06,000
Sir, please mind your hand.

2
00:00:24,450 --> 00:00:29,950
[Farrer Park Hospital]

3
00:01:04,780 --> 00:01:06,320
Morning.

4
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:08,950
- Morning.
- How are you feeling?

5
00:01:09,670 --> 00:01:11,250
Better.

6
00:01:11,250 --> 00:01:12,910
Sorry for collapsing yesterday.

7
00:01:12,910 --> 00:01:15,520
You don't need to apologize.

8
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:18,590
It's my duty to help you out.

9
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:26,000
For now, just focus on getting through
your first day at work.

10
00:01:26,650 --> 00:01:29,180
And contact me if anything happens.

11
00:01:29,180 --> 00:01:31,510
I'll come to you right away.

12
00:01:34,390 --> 00:01:37,800
- Have some breakfast.
- Thanks.

13
00:01:40,170 --> 00:01:42,450
I don't see the baby.

14
00:01:42,450 --> 00:01:43,860
Neither do I.

15
00:01:43,860 --> 00:01:46,170
They're in there somewhere.

16
00:01:47,010 --> 00:01:51,010
How about we change our point of view?

17
00:01:51,010 --> 00:01:53,140
Let's try looking from over there.

18
00:01:54,780 --> 00:01:56,550
Found them!

19
00:01:56,550 --> 00:02:02,830
Orangutans zip across the trees here,
just like in their natural habitats.

20
00:02:02,830 --> 00:02:05,020
So looking for them
is part of the experience.

21
00:02:05,020 --> 00:02:08,960
Indeed. It's rewarding
when you manage to find them.

22
00:02:09,930 --> 00:02:12,420
I see more over there!

23
00:02:14,700 --> 00:02:17,830
It's only your first day,
and you're already a pro.

24
00:02:17,830 --> 00:02:21,180
Thanks, but I have a ways to go.

25
00:02:27,460 --> 00:02:30,520
[Eita: How're you faring?]

26
00:03:11,580 --> 00:03:15,960
Sakura...

27
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:22,580
We're able to tour the gallery at 3PM...

28
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:27,210
I wasn't drawing some individual

29
00:03:30,110 --> 00:03:32,400
I only met yesterday.

30
00:03:34,420 --> 00:03:36,110
I've...

31
00:03:37,140 --> 00:03:39,990
I've always been drawing her.

32
00:03:50,140 --> 00:03:52,800
You know where this room is, don't you?

33
00:03:54,580 --> 00:03:56,330
She only looks similar to your muse.

34
00:04:00,480 --> 00:04:02,880
- I've heard enough.
- Where are you going?

35
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:04,420
Inside my sketches.

36
00:04:04,420 --> 00:04:07,050
Find that room, and you'll never come back.

37
00:04:12,550 --> 00:04:14,500
From where?

38
00:04:23,760 --> 00:04:26,820
We'll need to check the alleyway buildings.
[Katong Next Project]

39
00:04:26,820 --> 00:04:30,220
Ownership gets complicated there,
so some rooms are still furnished.

40
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:31,680
Have you asked the locals about them?

41
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:33,420
We're just about ready to do so.

42
00:04:33,420 --> 00:04:36,150
I'll handle that job.

43
00:04:36,150 --> 00:04:37,520
I want to survey the area anyway.

44
00:04:37,520 --> 00:04:39,570
But nothing's confirmed yet.

45
00:04:39,570 --> 00:04:42,820
It'll help to get a general feel
of the neighborhood.

46
00:04:42,820 --> 00:04:46,460
If you say so. Then we'll let you handle it.

47
00:04:46,460 --> 00:04:49,560
Lee, can you check plot 29?
[203]

48
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:51,400
Okay, Natsume.
[Artwork contact: TAN LEI]

49
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:55,470
The first half is a collaboration
with Mandai, so... landscapes.

50
00:04:55,470 --> 00:04:57,640
Then gradually, portraits.

51
00:04:57,640 --> 00:05:00,670
Please keep the last painting empty for now.

52
00:05:01,690 --> 00:05:04,020
A new piece at last?

53
00:05:05,140 --> 00:05:07,480
Yes.

54
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:09,530
I can't wait.

55
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:15,970
Excuse me.

56
00:05:15,970 --> 00:05:17,260
Yeah.

57
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:20,690
Hi, this is Tan Lei.

58
00:05:20,690 --> 00:05:23,710
This is Nishikido, from Junto Real Estate.

59
00:05:23,710 --> 00:05:28,330
I'd like to ask about
the artworks left in 203.

60
00:05:28,330 --> 00:05:30,160
<i>They're in storage.</i>

61
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:31,420
I see.

62
00:05:31,420 --> 00:05:35,050
Then could we arrange a time to check them?

63
00:05:53,350 --> 00:06:00,590
[Eita: Done with work? I can pick you up.]

64
00:06:00,590 --> 00:06:05,160
[It's fine. I'm heading straight home.]

65
00:06:06,170 --> 00:06:09,980
<i>For Katong, please transfer here.</i>

66
00:06:11,640 --> 00:06:17,690
[I'll be back after a slight detour.]

67
00:06:19,560 --> 00:06:23,060
[I'll be back after a slight detour.]

68
00:06:29,850 --> 00:06:33,690
[Location: Sakura]

69
00:06:42,670 --> 00:06:45,280
[Lei]

70
00:07:01,180 --> 00:07:03,100
Welcome.

71
00:07:05,630 --> 00:07:07,710
Is Lun here?

72
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:12,180
I see.

73
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:22,780
You... wait?

74
00:07:25,160 --> 00:07:27,290
Coffee?

75
00:07:27,290 --> 00:07:29,040
Yes.

76
00:07:42,160 --> 00:07:44,040
Thank you.

77
00:07:53,210 --> 00:07:57,490
I knew it. I know this flavor.

78
00:08:04,540 --> 00:08:08,490
I was here, four years ago...

79
00:08:08,490 --> 00:08:10,060
Maybe.

80
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:13,200
But I don't remember.

81
00:08:19,620 --> 00:08:21,980
You know this key, right?

82
00:08:25,510 --> 00:08:29,120
You know it, right?

83
00:08:34,860 --> 00:08:39,720
Some things are better left unknown.

84
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:50,700
Something is there.

85
00:09:09,160 --> 00:09:11,680
My body remembers.

86
00:10:26,670 --> 00:10:28,250
Woah!

87
00:10:31,760 --> 00:10:33,640
I know this place.

88
00:10:35,180 --> 00:10:39,010
Hello, I left my sketchbook here yesterday...

89
00:10:43,520 --> 00:10:45,520
Is she here?

90
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:46,980
She just left.

91
00:10:46,980 --> 00:10:48,720
Where did she go?

92
00:11:02,270 --> 00:11:05,040
I see you also can't help but look.

93
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:12,230
You know of this key, yes?

94
00:11:18,230 --> 00:11:22,050
You're better off knowing no more.

95
00:11:23,930 --> 00:11:26,350
If you truly believe so,

96
00:11:27,360 --> 00:11:29,980
why look so distraught?

97
00:11:34,250 --> 00:11:38,660
203 isn't a room number.

98
00:11:38,660 --> 00:11:41,900
It's the name of an old building

99
00:11:41,900 --> 00:11:45,700
that was managed by my late husband.

100
00:11:45,700 --> 00:11:50,060
And I resided there?

101
00:11:53,970 --> 00:11:56,140
It was your atelier.

102
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:59,550
And, a place you called home.

103
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:02,200
Did she also live there?

104
00:12:08,640 --> 00:12:11,000
You really shouldn't go.

105
00:12:15,590 --> 00:12:21,240
She should already be there, right?

106
00:13:36,050 --> 00:13:38,120
[Buy coffee beans before we run out]

107
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:40,140
[Don't put laundry away
while it's still damp]

108
00:13:40,140 --> 00:13:42,160
[Soak the dishes before washing]

109
00:13:48,550 --> 00:13:50,430
This is my handwriting.

110
00:14:13,300 --> 00:14:15,200
Sakura.

111
00:14:15,870 --> 00:14:17,170
Lun.

112
00:14:59,130 --> 00:15:01,040
This is the place.

113
00:15:01,040 --> 00:15:02,370
Huh?

114
00:15:06,010 --> 00:15:08,840
This is the place I've been drawing.

115
00:15:08,840 --> 00:15:10,960
I used to paint here.

116
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:19,850
But... I don't remember anything
from four years ago.

117
00:15:19,850 --> 00:15:21,510
Me too.

118
00:15:23,270 --> 00:15:24,960
You too?

119
00:15:26,550 --> 00:15:29,710
We lived here?

120
00:15:31,880 --> 00:15:33,840
I think so.

121
00:15:38,440 --> 00:15:40,480
<i>"Sorry."</i>

122
00:15:40,480 --> 00:15:41,860
<i>Is it the same meaning?</i>

123
00:15:41,860 --> 00:15:44,190
<i>Yes. Same meaning.</i>

124
00:16:07,520 --> 00:16:09,730
Still your spot?

125
00:16:09,730 --> 00:16:12,800
But this side is bigger.

126
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:16,140
Maybe you wanted to be near me?

127
00:16:16,140 --> 00:16:19,150
Maybe, you wanted to draw near me.

128
00:16:20,350 --> 00:16:24,640
Yeah, you're right.
Maybe I wanted to be near you.

129
00:16:27,900 --> 00:16:32,900
I wonder how we lived here?

130
00:16:34,100 --> 00:16:36,470
You used to scold me a lot.

131
00:16:40,680 --> 00:16:42,700
Look at the notes over there.

132
00:17:06,350 --> 00:17:07,730
Sorry.

133
00:17:07,730 --> 00:17:11,070
You just spoke Japanese.

134
00:17:11,070 --> 00:17:12,680
Huh?

135
00:17:12,680 --> 00:17:16,070
Right, why did I speak in Japanese?

136
00:17:18,240 --> 00:17:21,580
I think I used to say that,
when you looked angry.

137
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:24,450
Angry now?

138
00:17:26,540 --> 00:17:28,010
Nope.

139
00:17:37,140 --> 00:17:38,950
Lei?

140
00:17:38,950 --> 00:17:40,530
Let's go.

141
00:17:43,160 --> 00:17:46,340
You knew this place, didn't you?

142
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:54,190
Let's go.

143
00:17:54,190 --> 00:17:56,550
Why didn't you ever tell me?

144
00:17:59,390 --> 00:18:01,080
Lun!

145
00:18:03,050 --> 00:18:05,290
What happened to us?

146
00:18:05,290 --> 00:18:07,860
I don't remember anything.

147
00:18:07,860 --> 00:18:09,440
Really?

148
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:12,460
I see.

149
00:18:14,660 --> 00:18:18,460
So you got the chance to forget.

150
00:18:18,460 --> 00:18:21,180
- Lei.
- You know,

151
00:18:21,180 --> 00:18:23,640
even after you forgot,

152
00:18:24,460 --> 00:18:26,220
Lun...

153
00:18:26,220 --> 00:18:31,940
He kept painting this room over,
and over, and over again, for four years.

154
00:18:31,940 --> 00:18:35,700
Four years, someone with no name or face.

155
00:18:35,700 --> 00:18:39,050
- I'm sorry.
- Don't apologize.

156
00:18:39,050 --> 00:18:41,760
You don't remember, right?

157
00:18:43,840 --> 00:18:48,450
Lun. Leave now, and you can still...

158
00:18:49,920 --> 00:18:52,410
Still, what?

159
00:18:52,410 --> 00:18:55,150
He shouldn't come back here.

160
00:18:55,150 --> 00:18:56,220
Why?

161
00:18:56,220 --> 00:18:58,670
Because coming back here would...

162
00:18:58,670 --> 00:19:01,310
It would break him.

163
00:19:01,310 --> 00:19:02,980
Hold on.

164
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,970
Break me?

165
00:19:07,630 --> 00:19:09,470
Both of you.

166
00:19:16,260 --> 00:19:18,030
Can you wait here?

167
00:19:29,970 --> 00:19:31,550
Over here.

168
00:19:34,210 --> 00:19:35,800
Sakura.

169
00:19:37,870 --> 00:19:39,710
I came to get you.

170
00:19:40,790 --> 00:19:42,120
Sorry.

171
00:19:42,120 --> 00:19:45,840
I told you, no need to apologize.

172
00:19:47,450 --> 00:19:48,980
Let's go home.

173
00:19:53,530 --> 00:19:55,070
Sakura!

174
00:19:58,980 --> 00:20:00,940
She's tired.

175
00:20:15,140 --> 00:20:17,080
Are you thirsty?

176
00:20:17,080 --> 00:20:19,830
No, I'm fine.

177
00:20:23,080 --> 00:20:24,690
Then are you hungry?

178
00:20:24,690 --> 00:20:26,760
I can make us something when we get back.

179
00:20:27,450 --> 00:20:31,000
Okay. Thanks.

180
00:22:09,330 --> 00:22:10,980
Eita?

181
00:22:11,840 --> 00:22:14,980
Sorry. I was worried, so...

182
00:22:16,480 --> 00:22:18,450
You saw?

183
00:22:18,450 --> 00:22:20,580
You kept it.

184
00:22:30,280 --> 00:22:32,460
Eat, breakfast will get cold.

185
00:22:43,230 --> 00:22:45,330
What do you know?

186
00:22:45,870 --> 00:22:48,990
I knew about the man named Lun.

187
00:22:48,990 --> 00:22:50,940
Did you also know about 203?

188
00:22:51,660 --> 00:22:53,450
Yeah.

189
00:22:53,450 --> 00:22:55,010
For how long?

190
00:22:55,010 --> 00:22:57,440
Since before we started dating.

191
00:22:57,440 --> 00:23:00,390
Why didn't you ever tell me?

192
00:23:00,390 --> 00:23:03,620
Because you said you didn't want to remember.

193
00:23:04,900 --> 00:23:13,010
[Next]
